<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  RM_WebworkFauna.xml                    RM_Webwork · WEBWORK_FAUNA_ROSTER_1
  ============================================================================
  The 5 invented Webwork fauna rows per
  design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/webwork_fauna_roster_2026-09-23.md — the
  resident cast besides the Ollathrix (that species is out of scope, owned by
  webwork_owner_and_nest_2026-09-23.md): quarrok (row 1, anchor war),
  vennick (row 2, egg war), skennet/cravvet (rows 3-4, trace prey), sivvern
  (row 5, trace flier, real flight per the standing rule).

  Replaces the vanilla-Core wildAnimals placeholder (Rat/Hare/Muffalo/Cobra/
  Megaspider) RM_Webwork_Biome.xml shipped at scaffold time — that placeholder
  comment named this item by name as the thing that would replace it.
  🔑 "5 rows, no filler... the near-emptiness IS the design" (roster doc READ
  FIRST) — this is the WHOLE cast, not an addition to the vanilla rows.

  Donor-cut disposition (roster doc §7, all 4 RULED CUT by question card,
  2026-09-24, ledger note on this item discharging the 4th): Wyyyschokk,
  RSW_JewelBeetle, Kreetle/RSW_Kreetle, Shyrack. None of the 4 are wired here
  or via src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Patches/WildAnimals_Webwork.xml (edited
  this same pass to remove them) — RM_Quarrok explicitly supersedes
  RSW_JewelBeetle's interim chew-behaviour body (roster doc row 1 "replaces"
  field); RSW_JewelBeetle itself is untouched and remains wired at RUT_FeverWood
  0.2 per MIASMA_FEVERWOOD_GREENTIDE_BMT_1 — a cut here is not a leak there
  (owner ruling 2026-09-21). The frozen RUT_Webwork.xml twin is UNCHANGED and
  still carries all 4 donor rows on the live world until the terminal paint
  (BIOME_PAINT_ONCE_AT_THE_END_1) — none of this touches it.

  Bodies: quarrok/BeetleLikeWithClaw (shear-jaw mandibles, already used
  elsewhere in this repo — grep-confirmed valid); vennick/BeetleLike (tiny,
  same insect family, no claw); skennet/QuadrupedAnimalWithHooves (stilt-legged
  pale runner, same family this repo's other fast grazers use); cravvet/
  TurtleLike (squat domed sheller, same body Sump's skarrid already ships);
  sivvern/Bird (the biome's one flier, same body Sump's skellarn and TheForge's
  fleet flier already ship).

  Art: none of the five has existing generated art anywhere (registry.jsonl/
  done/_artsrc searched this pass, 0 hits on all five names — sanity-probed
  against "graniteslug", 12/30 hits depending on instrument, so the search
  itself is live, per confident-wrong-numbers). Flat-colour placeholders
  generated this pass (art/Fauna/gen_webwork_fauna_placeholder.py) so none of
  the five renders magenta; real art queued
  (infrastructure/artpipe/art_lists/webwork_fauna.csv, 15 pending jobs,
  south/east/north per generating-rimworld-sprites). Never blocks load.

  Mechanism scope — deferred, same convention as SUMP_FAUNA_ROSTER_1's own
  header ("content-complete... bespoke behaviours are follow-on mechanics
  work"): quarrok's RM_ChewAnchorsConsumerExtension marker + the
  Animal_PreWander splice (RM_ThinkTree_ChewAnchors.xml) ARE built this pass —
  the mechanism was shipped with no consumer race (WEBWORK_KIT_BUILD_1) and
  this row is explicitly named as that consumer (roster doc row 1). Vennick's
  RM_JobGiver_RunToEggs ("the living treasure map") is the doc's own "owed" —
  NOT built here; until it exists vennick is a content-complete ordinary prey
  animal with no bespoke pathing. Sivvern's prey preference for vennick and
  its flight animation flip-book are likewise not built — vanilla predator
  behaviour covers the former, and GetBestFlyAnimation returns null with no
  frames set, which is correct and never blocks flight.

  Flight (RM_Sivvern only): real flight per the standing rule (owner,
  2026-09-19) — MaxFlightTime/FlightCooldown are the CORE stat pair
  (Pawn_FlightTracker.CanEverFly), not a bool. canLeaveMapFlying deliberately
  OMITTED: the roster doc's own one-home note says it lairs in the sealed
  canopy, no migration mechanism claimed ("the flier carve-out is narrow and
  this row does not invoke it"). Numbers are the roster doc's own "❓"
  estimates (~8 MaxFlightTime, ~5 FlightCooldown, ~2.5 flightSpeedFactor),
  landed as real values since a def field cannot ship a question mark — same
  posture as RM_SumpFauna's RM_Skellarn, the closest sibling precedent.

  Commonalities/ecoSystemWeight/wildGroupSize below are engineering defaults
  (roster doc gives silhouette/role, not tuned numbers), not owner-set values.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Defs>

  <!-- =================================================================
       QUARROK — the anchor war (row 1)
       WAR: hates the spiders instinctively, chews web anchors, slowly
       undoing the networks. USE: herdable corridor-cutter — beetle-cut
       anchors deregister SenseWeb cells, making a blind corridor.
       Neutral, never fights the Ollathrix; not a guard animal.
       ================================================================= -->

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_Quarrok</defName>
    <label>quarrok</label>
    <description>A great slab-backed jungle beetle, dull bronze-black under a dusting of silk lint, jaws like shears — unhurried, unbothered, and always at work on an anchor. It hates the web on some level too deep to reason with, and will spend a whole day cutting through a single silk line. It never troubles anything with legs.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>2.4</MoveSpeed>
      <MarketValue>65</MarketValue>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>0.25</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>0.1</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <Wildness>0.6</Wildness>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mandibles</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>9</power>
        <cooldownTime>2</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <race>
      <body>BeetleLikeWithClaw</body>
      <baseBodySize>1.4</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>1.2</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.3</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>VegetarianRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <fleshType>Insectoid</fleshType>
      <bloodDef>Filth_BloodInsect</bloodDef>
      <bloodSmearDef>Filth_BloodSmear</bloodSmearDef>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0.05</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <!-- Herdable via the roster doc's "living-tool" lure pattern, not tame
           commands (row 1's own war/use field: "not a battle-pet"). No
           herdAnimal-driven grouping mechanism is built here — deferred with
           the rest of the herding behaviour. -->
      <lifeExpectancy>10</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>10</gestationPeriodDays>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.3</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.6</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <butcherProducts>
        <RM_QuarrokChitin>4</RM_QuarrokChitin>
      </butcherProducts>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
    </race>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- WEBWORK_FAUNA_ROSTER_1: gives RM_JobGiver_ChewAnchors (shipped by
           WEBWORK_KIT_BUILD_1 with no consumer race) its first consumer. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_ChewAnchorsConsumerExtension" />
    </modExtensions>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalUncommon</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

